#
# OCI 11.2's `declare r sys_refcursor := :1; n number; begin fetch r into n;
# :2 := n; end;` with the open cursor bound IN (#2466): its descriptor the OUT
# form's, a REF CURSOR (102) of one byte; its value the cursor's id, 3, as a
# 4-byte value, where the OUT form sends 0.
# Captured 2026-11-07 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, the client charset AL32UTF8; a statement
# handle opened by a block's SQLT_RSET OUT bind, then bound SQLT_RSET IN to a
# second block by OCIBindByPos, called through ctypes) on Oracle 11g XE
# 11.2.0.2 with SERVER=POOLED, the DRCP pool started. The TTC payload, without
# the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the
# |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
